module contract;

// Card W45-CONTRACT-REVISION-MODE: every contract in this module is
// `revision flexible` (contract spec C06.2): it binds by name and declared
// signature at any revision of the audited project, and reports list the libc
// contracts as one standing assumption, the libc/C-standard ABI premise. The
// C library's version stays in the build's provenance.

// The C library's `errno` accessor — resource-projection vocabulary version 1.
//
// Card CONSTRUCTOR-RESIDUALS. This module declares a TRUSTED ASSUMPTION about
// one C library function. It verifies nothing: no C body is analyzed by this
// loader, and a declaration is a premise.
//
// ## What the call sites actually reach — measured, not assumed
//
// `errno` is not an object in any translation unit of the pinned corpus. C11
// 7.5p2 permits it to be "a modifiable lvalue ... that expands to a modifiable
// lvalue", and glibc defines it as a macro over a function call
// (`/usr/include/errno.h:37-38` on the audited host):
//
//     extern int *__errno_location (void) __THROW __attribute_const__;
//     # define errno (*__errno_location ())
//
// So every `errno` a preprocessed unit of this corpus contains is the token
// sequence `( * __errno_location ( ) )`, and the callee the resource
// projection sees is `__errno_location`.
//
// ## `__errno_location`, read from its declaration
//
//   int *__errno_location (void)
//
//   * It takes NO parameters, so no argument of any caller can reach it and no
//     caller's custody obligation can be affected through one.
//   * It returns a pointer to the calling thread's `errno` object. That object
//     has static storage duration and thread-local lifetime (C11 7.5p2): it is
//     not allocated by this call, it is not the caller's to free, and no
//     library function in this corpus frees it. The caller therefore acquires
//     NO obligation, which is exactly `resource_return_none()`.
//   * `__THROW` and `__attribute_const__` carry no type and no effect this
//     projection models.
//
// The result type is spelled `ptr<mut, u8>` because that is this vocabulary's
// projection of every single-`*` non-`const` pointer (`POINTER_ABI_TYPES`); the
// declared *pointee* is deliberately not spelled here, and the gateway reads it
// from the unit's own declarations instead — see below.
//
// ## What this declaration does NOT admit on its own
//
// Declaring `__errno_location` does not make `errno` readable anywhere. The
// gateway's dereference-of-a-call-result rule (card CONSTRUCTOR-RESIDUALS,
// premises N1-N10) independently requires, PER CALL SITE, that the call is the
// statement's only nested call, that it occupies a whole argument at a declared
// `Borrowed` position modulo the dereference wrapper, that its written arity
// equals this declaration's, and — premise N10 — that THIS TRANSLATION UNIT's
// own declaration of the callee returns exactly one `*` over a scalar type.
// A unit that declares `__errno_location` differently, or does not declare it
// at all, refuses every such site under this declaration exactly as without it.
//
// Card VERDICT-CONTRACT-PREMISE-ANNOTATIONS: stated on `__errno_location` as
// `requires resource_premise(nested_call_admission, "...")` (contract spec
// C04.18), so every verdict that rests on the declaration names it.
//
// ## What no declaration here says
//
// Nothing about the value of `errno`, nothing about which library functions set
// it, nothing about the ordering of a set against a read, and nothing about
// thread-local storage lifetime beyond the caller acquiring no obligation.
// This is a per-call custody statement about the CALLER's obligations, and
// nothing more.
//
// ## Portability, recorded rather than assumed
//
// `__errno_location` is the glibc spelling. musl declares the same name; macOS
// spells it `__error()` and Windows `_errno()`. On a host whose headers use a
// different spelling this declaration names a function no analysed unit
// contains, so it is inert text there — the same measured-inert situation card
// PROD-CONTRACTS recorded for `flb_trace`, and harmless for the same reason.

extern fn __errno_location() -> ptr<mut, u8>
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    requires resource_revision(flexible);
    requires resource_premise(nested_call_admission, "a dereference of this call's result is read only where the gateway's nested-call admission holds at the call site (premises N1-N10 of cards O04-TRACE and CONSTRUCTOR-RESIDUALS, checked per site): the call is the statement's only nested call and a whole argument of a contracted call at a declared Borrowed position modulo the dereference wrapper (N4-D), its written arity is this declaration's, and the unit's own declaration of the callee returns exactly one pointer level over a scalar type (N10); under them the argument binds, releases, escapes and addresses nothing the projection tracks");
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};

// ## `strerror` (card W44-LIBC-RESIDUALS, `LIBC-PRINTF-NESTED-TAIL-CALLEES`)
//
// TRUSTED ASSUMPTION (trust boundary 28). Declared in `<string.h>`, and placed
// beside the `errno` accessor it serves rather than in `libc/string.qcore`,
// which is a PUBLISHED module whose SHA-256 every inheriting contract's
// identity carries (`providers/contract-load-path.json`): appending there would
// move that identity for a declaration no inheriting contract uses. Read from
// the prototype the analysed units declare (`/usr/include/string.h`):
//
//   extern char *strerror (int __errnum) __THROW;
//
//   * `__errnum` is an `int` by value: `resource_borrowed`.
//   * The result points to a message the caller must NOT free: glibc returns a
//     string in static read-only storage, or one in a thread-local buffer the
//     next `strerror` call on that thread may overwrite. Nothing is allocated
//     for the caller and the result points into no argument, so the caller
//     acquires no obligation: `resource_return_none()`, the precedent
//     `gai_strerror` (`libc/socket.qcore`), `dlerror` (`libc/dlfcn.qcore`) and
//     `__errno_location` above set for a pointer result with no custody.
//
// Measured use: two printf-family tails pass `strerror(r)` whole, where the
// nested-call admission (card O04-TRACE's premises N3, N6 and N7) needs exactly
// this declaration. The census agrees in all 181 units that declare it.
// Nothing about the message's lifetime past the next call, its text, locale or
// `errno` is stated.
//
// Card VERDICT-CONTRACT-PREMISE-ANNOTATIONS: stated on `strerror` as `requires
// resource_premise(nested_call_admission, "...")` (contract spec C04.18), so
// every verdict that rests on the declaration names it.

extern fn strerror(errnum: i32) -> ptr<mut, u8>
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    requires resource_revision(flexible);
    requires resource_premise(nested_call_admission, "a call of this function nested whole in another call's argument is read only where card O04-TRACE's nested-call admission holds at the call site; this declaration meets its premises N3 (a contract in force), N6 (result mode None) and N7 (every parameter Borrowed), and the admission checks the rest per site");
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(errnum);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};
